### 3. Backend Authorization Middleware & Controller Endpoints

#### [MODIFY] [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/src/middleware/auth.js)
* Create `requireModeratorPermission(moduleName, action)` middleware:
  * If `req.user.role === 'ADMIN'`: automatically grant access.
  * If `req.user.role !== 'MODERATOR'`: return `403 Forbidden` (`FORBIDDEN_ROLE`).
  * Parse `req.user.moderatorPermissions`.
  * If `permissions[moduleName]?.[action] === true`: allow request.
  * Otherwise: return `403 Forbidden` with a descriptive message (`Access denied. Missing permission: ${moduleName}.${action}`).

#### [MODIFY] [adminController.js](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/src/controllers/adminController.js)
* Add `updateModeratorPermissions`:
  * Validates the permission payload against the allowed matrix.
  * Compares previous permissions with new permissions.
  * Updates `user.moderatorPermissions` and sets `status = 'ACTIVE'` if previously pending.
  * Records detailed audit log entries into `AuditLog` for each toggled permission (capturing module, action, previous value, new value, admin email/ID, timestamp).
* Add `getModeratorPermissionHistory`:
  * Returns the audit log history filtered for `action = 'MODERATOR_PERMISSION_CHANGED'` on that specific user.

#### [MODIFY] [adminRoutes.js](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/src/routes/adminRoutes.js)
* Register:
  * `PUT /api/v1/admin/users/:id/moderator-permissions`
  * `GET /api/v1/admin/users/:id/moderator-permissions/history`

#### [MODIFY] [moderatorRoutes.js](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/src/routes/moderatorRoutes.js)
